321 - My Jesus, I Love Thee
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 321
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[F]My Jesus, [Bb/F]I love [F]Thee, I know Thou [C7]art mine;
[C7]For Thee [F]all the follies [Bb/F]of sin [F]I resign.
[F]My gracious [C7]Redeemer, [F]my Savior art [Bb]Thou;
[Am]If [C7/G]ever [C/E]I loved [F]thee, my [Bb]Jesus, [F/C]'tis [C]now.

Verse 2:
[F]I love [Bb/F]thee because [F]thou hast first [C7]loved me,
[C7]and purchased [F]my pardon [Bb/F]on Calvary's [F]tree;
[F]I love [C7]thee for wearing [F]the thorns on thy [Bb]brow;
[Am]if [C7/G]ever [C/E]I loved [F]thee, my [Bb]Jesus, [F/C]'tis [C]now.

Verse 3:
[F]I'll love Thee [Bb/F]in life, [F]I will love Thee [C7]'til death,
[C7]And praise [F]Thee as long [Bb/F]as Thou lendest [F]me breath;
[F]And say [C7]when the death dew [F]lies cold on my [Bb]brow,
[Am]if [C7/G]ever [C/E]I loved [F]thee, my [Bb]Jesus, [F/C]'tis [C]now.

Verse 4:
[F]In mansions [Bb/F]of glory [F]and endless [C7]delight;
[C7]I'll ever [F]adore [Bb/F]thee in heaven [F]so bright;
[F]I'll sing [C7]with the glittering [F]crown on my [Bb]brow;
[Am]if [C7/G]ever [C/E]I loved [F]thee, my [Bb]Jesus, [F/C]'tis [C]now.
